From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:26:25 -0700
Subject: gpu: Check GL errors before marking CopySharedImage dest cleared

On Ganesh-GL, Skia does not surface GL driver errors from uploads or
draws. Drain GL errors before CopySharedImage writes to an uncleared
destination and verify none were raised before updating its cleared
rect, matching WritePixelsYUV. DrainGLErrors now accepts a null GLApi
so callers can skip the check without a separate guard.

Bug: 566384898
Change-Id: I0295859a32560e873c0ed5b335fdb5e792c2debb
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8530670
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1713877}

